Package: tppcm
Type: Package
Title: Step Discriminations for the Two-Parameter Partial Credit Model on Top of 'TAM'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jie-Wen", "Tsai", email = "tsai.jiewen@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for the two-parameter partial credit model (TPPCM; Yu,
    1991), in which every step of a polytomous item has its own discrimination. Estimation is
    left to existing software: 'TAM' (tam.mml.3pl() with a step design matrix,
    tam.mml.2pl(), tam.mml()) and, for the bilinear product form and
    non-negativity constraints, 'sirt' (xxirt()). The package adds what these
    packages do not provide: standard errors of step discriminations based on
    the full observed information, step-level Wald tests, and score tests with
    modification indices and expected parameter changes for moving down the
    model ladder saturated TPPCM -> product form -> GPCM -> PCM,
    limited-information fit statistics (M2, RMSEA, SRMSR, CFI, TLI;
    Maydeu-Olivares and Joe (2006) <doi:10.1007/s11336-005-1295-9>) for any
    step design, step contributions to the item information, and tests of
    differential step functioning across groups: per-step Lagrange multiplier
    tests from one multigroup fit (Glas, 1998), with the generalized score
    test of Boos (1992) <doi:10.1080/00031305.1992.10475921>, likelihood
    ratio tests with configural, metric, scalar and partial multigroup
    designs, score-based tests (Merkle and Zeileis (2013)
    <doi:10.1007/s11336-012-9302-4>) and model-based trees (Zeileis, Hothorn
    and Hornik (2008) <doi:10.1198/106186008X319331>). The generalized partial credit
    model of Muraki (1992) <doi:10.1177/014662169201600206> is the special
    case with equal steps within items.
